  data: {
    LLM: 'Identify tiles that can form a multiple of 10; use wilds 4-2 and 2-1 as 3 or 6 when needed.\n\nSplit the hand into odd- and even-pip tiles; (even+even+even), (odd+odd+even) can be multiples of 10; (odd+odd+odd) cannot.\n\nWith five odd tiles you cannot discard and lose; with four odds start from the one even tile; with three odds look for odd+odd+even; with two odds try two odds plus one even, or three evens; with one odd treat it as flexible; with no odds search among all five.',
    Player: 'Identify tiles that can form a multiple of 10; use wilds 4-2 and 2-1 as 3 or 6 when needed.\n\nSplit the hand into odd- and even-pip tiles; (even+even+even), (odd+odd+even) can be multiples of 10; (odd+odd+odd) cannot.\n\nWith five odd tiles you cannot discard and lose; with four odds start from the one even tile; with three odds look for odd+odd+even; with two odds try two odds plus one even, or three evens; with one odd treat it as flexible; with no odds search among all five.',
